WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.295
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.565 --> 00:08.074
I can't believe classes start next week!

3
00:08.075 --> 00:09.935
It went by so fast.

4
00:11.375 --> 00:12.375
Oh.

5
00:12.545 --> 00:14.691
Come on, one last trip to the beach before summer ends!

6
00:14.715 --> 00:17.445
Crowded places really aren't my thing...

7
00:17.475 --> 00:19.345
What are you talking about?

8
00:19.365 --> 00:20.744
Summer means going to the beach!

9
00:20.745 --> 00:21.985
Wait, really?

10
00:28.645 --> 00:29.645
What's wrong?

11
00:30.495 --> 00:31.425
Nothing.

12
00:31.425 --> 00:32.425
It's nothing.

13
00:41.405 --> 00:42.375
It really is Sae!

14
00:42.376 --> 00:44.224
Wait, it actually is Sae!

15
00:44.225 --> 00:46.785
Whoa, we haven't seen each other since middle school graduation!

16
00:47.705 --> 00:48.714
Oh, long time no see.

17
00:48.715 --> 00:49.944
You startled me.

18
00:49.945 --> 00:50.805
Whoa, your hair got so long!

19
00:50.905 --> 00:52.344
I didn't recognize you for a second.

20
00:52.345 --> 00:54.404
I mean, we only knew you back when you were 'Sae-kun.'

21
00:54.405 --> 00:55.215
Totally.

22
00:55.225 --> 00:56.284
Please, seriously, don't bring that up.

23
00:56.285 --> 00:57.764
That's my ultimate cringe phase.

24
00:57.765 --> 01:01.154
Aw, but I actually really liked the old Sae-kun.

25
01:01.155 --> 01:02.155
Yeah, me too.

26
01:03.825 --> 01:07.125
Knock it off, that's creepy.

27
01:07.165 --> 01:08.261
Aw, why? What's wrong with that?

28
01:08.285 --> 01:10.401
- Come on, it's not that big a deal. - So, how's college going for you two?

29
01:10.425 --> 01:11.425
We're getting by.

30
01:11.426 --> 01:12.935
Oh, really?

31
01:19.205 --> 01:20.442
(35th Class, Mine High Girls' Tennis Club) (Mukai Airi: How's everyone doing? We're having...

32
01:20.466 --> 01:21.704
a girls' tennis reunion in September! It's a joint one with the upperclassmen this time!)

33
01:21.705 --> 01:23.704
(Hinata: I heard Kumagai senpai is coming too!)

34
01:23.705 --> 01:26.145
(Kanon: Good for you, Miwa! You definitely have to come, lol)

35
02:07.505 --> 02:15.005
"How Do We Relationship?"

36
02:20.335 --> 02:23.875
(Episode 4: I Can't Touch You) It's so hot, I'm melting...

37
02:26.405 --> 02:28.275
That was such a surprise earlier.

38
02:28.715 --> 02:32.385
It's been forever since I ran into anyone from middle school.

39
02:32.845 --> 02:34.245
Yeah.

40
02:36.085 --> 02:38.255
Was 'Sae-kun' your old nickname?

41
02:39.455 --> 02:41.695
Sorry, can we just drop that?

42
02:46.325 --> 02:47.225
I'm sorry.

43
02:47.245 --> 02:48.995
It really was my ultimate cringe phase!

44
02:49.195 --> 02:51.915
You have embarrassing memories you'd rather forget too, right, Miwa?

45
02:54.005 --> 02:56.024
Well, yeah, a few...

46
02:56.025 --> 03:00.045
See? It's common courtesy not to dig them up.

47
03:00.475 --> 03:01.475
Case closed!

48
03:05.121 --> 03:06.115
Hey, by the way...

49
03:09.115 --> 03:11.385
Actually, lately...

50
03:11.555 --> 03:14.185
I think there's a high school reunion coming up for me, too.

51
03:14.695 --> 03:16.355
I'm on the fence about going.

52
03:16.595 --> 03:17.395
Huh?

53
03:17.396 --> 03:19.195
Why? You should go.

54
03:21.195 --> 03:23.935
Someone I used to have a crush on might be there...

55
03:26.125 --> 03:28.735
Of course, I don't feel that way about her anymore at all.

56
03:30.305 --> 03:32.044
Then what's the problem?

57
03:32.045 --> 03:33.045
Just go.

58
03:34.715 --> 03:35.715
But...

59
03:37.545 --> 03:39.115
What, are you worrying about me?

60
03:39.165 --> 03:40.661
It's not like anything's gonna happen, right?

61
03:40.685 --> 03:44.455
Or do you still have lingering feelings for your ex-crush?

62
03:46.255 --> 03:47.255
No way! Of course not!

63
03:48.525 --> 03:49.525
Well...

64
03:50.395 --> 03:52.725
All right, I guess I'll go.

65
03:54.065 --> 03:55.065
Yeah.

66
03:55.365 --> 03:56.465
Take care.

67
04:05.445 --> 04:06.405
Great rehearsal, everyone!

68
04:06.406 --> 04:07.545
Great work, everyone!

69
04:07.815 --> 04:09.651
Wait, did Ryu get his groove back or something?

70
04:09.675 --> 04:10.875
You bet!

71
04:10.945 --> 04:12.785
After summer break comes the campus festival!

72
04:12.945 --> 04:14.484
And the festival means a live gig!

73
04:14.485 --> 04:16.285
And a live gig means...?

74
04:16.585 --> 04:17.785
Getting popular!

75
04:17.825 --> 04:18.884
We'll be so popular!

76
04:18.885 --> 04:20.385
I see how it is.

77
04:21.925 --> 04:23.095
Um, guys...

78
04:23.525 --> 04:25.695
About the campus festival...

79
04:30.865 --> 04:33.535
(Lightning Rabbit) What if we try writing an original song?

80
04:34.745 --> 04:35.745
Huh?

81
04:35.905 --> 04:38.005
You mean write our own music?!

82
04:38.975 --> 04:42.145
It's a rare chance, so I thought we could give it a shot.

83
04:43.415 --> 04:45.615
I've never done that before.

84
04:45.745 --> 04:46.884
What about you, Mikkun?

85
04:46.885 --> 04:48.255
No, no, no way.

86
04:48.285 --> 04:51.015
Though honestly, I've always thought it sounded pretty cool.

87
04:52.405 --> 04:56.895
Does that mean... we write the lyrics, too?

88
04:57.125 --> 04:59.694
Hey, that sounds awesome!

89
04:59.695 --> 05:00.925
- It really does! - Right?

90
05:01.535 --> 05:05.035
Only if everyone's on board, of course.

91
05:14.445 --> 05:15.515
So, what do you think?

92
05:18.765 --> 05:22.585
I'm in!

93
05:24.925 --> 05:26.785
An original song, huh?

94
05:27.485 --> 05:30.225
Composing the music is one thing... Writing lyrics is tough, though.

95
05:30.555 --> 05:32.355
Hey Miwa, are you good at that kind of thing?

96
05:32.725 --> 05:33.725
Huh?

97
05:34.735 --> 05:35.835
I don't know...

98
05:36.145 --> 05:37.095
Well, um...

99
05:37.096 --> 05:39.535
I did always like literature class back in school.

100
05:40.265 --> 05:42.805
You have that poetic vibe. I bet you could do it.

101
05:42.941 --> 05:44.181
What's that supposed to mean?!

102
05:44.545 --> 05:46.505
Just kidding!

103
05:57.855 --> 05:58.955
Hey, um...

104
05:59.355 --> 06:00.655
Saeko.

105
06:03.855 --> 06:04.865
Tonight...

106
06:05.365 --> 06:06.665
I want to be the one.

107
06:09.195 --> 06:10.195
Huh?

108
06:10.535 --> 06:12.035
What... What are you saying?

109
06:13.185 --> 06:14.185
I mean...

110
06:14.835 --> 06:15.835
Well...

111
06:17.535 --> 06:18.745
I want to hold you.

112
06:18.975 --> 06:20.275
I want to hold you, Saeko.

113
06:21.915 --> 06:23.315
I want you to let me hold you.

114
06:24.885 --> 06:25.885
Can't I?

115
06:29.285 --> 06:30.745
No, no, no, no, no!

116
06:30.755 --> 06:31.685
No way, no way, no way!

117
06:31.725 --> 06:34.355
Absolutely not! Okay, time for you to go home!

118
06:34.725 --> 06:36.695
You don't have to reject me so harshly!

119
06:36.995 --> 06:38.805
No means no!

120
06:39.395 --> 06:40.395
Besides...

121
06:40.725 --> 06:42.405
Where is this coming from all of a sudden?

122
06:43.135 --> 06:44.805
It's not sudden at all.

123
06:45.465 --> 06:47.235
I've always wanted to...

124
06:47.905 --> 06:50.405
But you never let me touch you.

125
06:51.375 --> 06:53.375
You always keep your clothes on.

126
06:56.615 --> 06:58.415
I don't need that...

127
07:00.215 --> 07:01.215
But...

128
07:01.685 --> 07:03.485
Saeko, you said it yourself before...

129
07:06.755 --> 07:09.695
That you... you have a sex drive, too, right?

130
07:10.655 --> 07:13.094
It's not about having a sex drive.

131
07:13.095 --> 07:15.045
It's just... I can't do it!

132
07:16.071 --> 07:18.611
I just can't imagine letting someone hold me.

133
07:18.635 --> 07:19.635
Why not?

134
07:24.805 --> 07:28.245
Hearing myself pant creeps me out...

135
07:29.615 --> 07:33.115
And I could never let my guard down enough to moan like an idiot.

136
07:34.515 --> 07:35.855
What's that supposed to mean?

137
07:36.915 --> 07:39.285
Are you saying I look like an idiot when we do it?

138
07:39.305 --> 07:40.324
Wait, no! That's not what I meant!

139
07:40.325 --> 07:42.794
Miwa, you're different! You're cute, so it works!

140
07:42.795 --> 07:43.355
Right?

141
07:43.395 --> 07:44.395
Whatever, forget it!

142
07:44.665 --> 07:46.265
Miwa...

143
08:12.085 --> 08:13.285
Miwa...

144
08:14.185 --> 08:16.625
Why are you okay with being held like that?

145
08:18.695 --> 08:19.695
Well...

146
08:20.065 --> 08:21.935
I never really thought about it...

147
08:23.195 --> 08:26.405
Someone else is doing whatever they want with your body, you know?

148
08:27.805 --> 08:28.635
Yeah...

149
08:28.805 --> 08:32.475
Of course it's embarrassing.

150
08:34.105 --> 08:37.015
But you tell me I'm cute...

151
08:40.085 --> 08:42.755
...and you accept all of me.

152
08:43.555 --> 08:46.325
That's why I can trust you and give myself over to you.

153
09:05.685 --> 09:06.785
Miwa...!

154
09:08.545 --> 09:11.615
Next time, you can hold me...!

155
09:26.665 --> 09:28.634
No. The mood is completely ruined for tonight.

156
09:28.635 --> 09:29.715
Let's just call it a night.

157
09:30.335 --> 09:31.335
Sorry...

158
09:32.905 --> 09:34.204
I'll buy you a treat sometime.

159
09:34.205 --> 09:35.205
Thanks.

160
09:41.175 --> 09:43.775
If you really don't want to, just tell her straight up.

161
09:44.625 --> 09:47.445
Like, 'I'm not mentally ready for that yet.'

162
09:47.985 --> 09:49.915
That feels so unfair to her, though...

163
09:50.785 --> 09:53.625
I don't want our relationship to stay one-sided forever.

164
09:55.625 --> 09:56.625
Hey.

165
09:57.255 --> 09:59.025
Just out of curiosity...

166
09:59.425 --> 10:00.865
Why won't you take off your clothes?

167
10:02.365 --> 10:03.464
What do you mean, 'why'?

168
10:03.465 --> 10:05.634
Come on, doesn't it make you want to strip down even more?

169
10:05.635 --> 10:06.924
I know I do!

170
10:06.925 --> 10:08.805
Especially in front of someone I like.

171
10:08.905 --> 10:10.774
Like, baring it all and laying your cards on the table?

172
10:10.775 --> 10:12.215
What cards are you even laying down?

173
10:13.475 --> 10:15.345
Seriously, though...

174
10:15.415 --> 10:17.175
What's the real reason?

175
10:18.865 --> 10:20.245
Well...

176
10:21.415 --> 10:22.615
I just feel like...

177
10:23.455 --> 10:26.485
I can't stand the whole situation.

178
10:27.055 --> 10:29.528
It feels like this hyper-rational version of me watching from the sidelines thinking,

179
10:29.552 --> 10:32.025
'Why are you getting turned on? It's gross.' And that just kills the mood completely.

180
10:33.465 --> 10:35.235
I see.

181
10:36.435 --> 10:37.435
Yeah.

182
10:37.665 --> 10:39.665
I don't get it at all.

183
10:42.575 --> 10:44.575
Wait, come to think of it...

184
10:44.945 --> 10:47.185
Why do I want to take my clothes off in the first place?

185
10:47.345 --> 10:48.945
How should I know?

186
10:49.175 --> 10:51.185
Huh, good point.

187
10:51.985 --> 10:54.455
Now I feel stupid for overthinking this...

188
10:54.585 --> 10:55.644
What are we even talking about?

189
10:55.645 --> 10:57.055
Seriously.

190
10:58.825 --> 11:00.155
Ugh...

191
11:01.825 --> 11:03.255
What's up, Sae-chan?

192
11:04.565 --> 11:07.065
Nothing. I was just zoning out for a second.

193
11:07.425 --> 11:09.265
Need help with anything?

194
11:09.895 --> 11:10.895
No, I'm good.

195
11:13.305 --> 11:14.775
You've got this face right now...

196
11:15.005 --> 11:18.624
like it's not your first time, but it's the day you're gearing up to have sex for the first time.

197
11:18.625 --> 11:19.675
Totally that kind of face.

198
11:19.845 --> 11:20.845
Excuse me?!

199
11:20.905 --> 11:23.065
What are you talking about?! That's sexual harassment!

200
11:23.375 --> 11:26.445
Hey, my intuition is usually spot on, so I had to ask.

201
11:30.515 --> 11:31.985
All right, Kamedo-san...

202
11:32.485 --> 11:36.025
Can you tell what kind of person I'm dating right now?

203
11:36.805 --> 11:39.325
Hmm, let me think.

204
11:40.525 --> 11:42.265
Pretty clingy...

205
11:43.765 --> 11:45.605
...high-maintenance and intense...

206
11:46.735 --> 11:49.935
...and prefers giving love over receiving it. That kind of... guy.

207
11:50.675 --> 11:52.245
Wrong!

208
11:52.265 --> 11:53.644
Dead wrong!

209
11:53.645 --> 11:55.914
Strange. My gut is usually never off.

210
11:55.915 --> 11:56.975
Too bad, so sad.

211
11:57.015 --> 11:58.615
I'm going to wipe tables now.

212
11:59.505 --> 12:02.655
You know, Sae-chan, you're really good at playing it cool.

213
12:05.955 --> 12:08.755
Like I said, you haven't gotten a single thing right.

214
12:13.765 --> 12:15.835
Sorry I'm late!

215
12:15.865 --> 12:17.735
No worries. Thanks for working so hard today.

216
12:17.935 --> 12:19.805
I'm totally beat!

217
12:20.605 --> 12:22.305
Look, swings!

218
12:22.375 --> 12:23.455
Let's go on them for a bit!

219
12:40.605 --> 12:42.864
Saeko, didn't you just say you were exhausted?

220
12:42.865 --> 12:44.825
Swings are fun, come on!

221
12:45.125 --> 12:47.795
Oh, I used to stand on these when I was a kid.

222
12:50.165 --> 12:52.935
You seem kind of hyper today.

223
12:58.075 --> 12:59.575
That's rare for you.

224
12:59.605 --> 13:01.545
You didn't put on any nail polish today.

225
13:02.245 --> 13:03.245
Oh.

226
13:04.065 --> 13:05.065
Yeah.

227
13:05.705 --> 13:06.705
Because...

228
13:07.415 --> 13:08.885
We can do it tonight, right?

229
13:09.855 --> 13:11.925
I thought it'd be better to leave them bare.

230
13:12.625 --> 13:13.685
Oh...

231
13:14.505 --> 13:15.895
I see...

232
13:23.065 --> 13:24.365
Hey, Saeko.

233
13:27.005 --> 13:28.135
This is for you.

234
13:28.405 --> 13:29.405
Huh?

235
13:40.285 --> 13:42.285
It's so cute...

236
13:42.615 --> 13:43.615
Wait a second...

237
13:43.815 --> 13:45.161
Isn't this a little too cute for me?

238
13:45.185 --> 13:46.585
You should wear it, Miwa.

239
13:48.095 --> 13:49.295
Actually...

240
13:49.825 --> 13:51.125
I got one, too.

241
13:55.195 --> 13:58.705
Isn't wearing matching jewelry a bit embarrassing?

242
14:02.375 --> 14:03.705
If you don't like it...

243
14:04.205 --> 14:06.305
...we don't have to wear them on the same day.

244
14:06.345 --> 14:08.645
It's not that I hate it...

245
14:10.375 --> 14:11.645
I just wanted to...

246
14:12.145 --> 14:15.085
...do cute girlfriend stuff once in a while.

247
14:17.825 --> 14:19.025
All right, all right.

248
14:25.625 --> 14:27.125
We should head back soon.

249
14:28.325 --> 14:29.325
Hey, um...

250
14:31.725 --> 14:34.905
Can I make one selfish request?

251
14:36.705 --> 14:37.705
Hm?

252
14:38.575 --> 14:40.805
Could we go to a love hotel nearby?

253
14:41.815 --> 14:42.815
Why...?

254
14:43.945 --> 14:44.945
I don't know...

255
14:45.765 --> 14:48.155
I feel like an unfamiliar place might be easier.

256
14:48.305 --> 14:51.285
If we're at your place, I might get stuck in my head.

257
14:52.225 --> 14:53.785
You don't have to force yourself if you don't want to...

258
14:53.805 --> 14:55.005
It's not that I don't want to.

259
14:55.395 --> 14:58.825
And if I can't even do this for you...

260
15:00.225 --> 15:02.025
...what kind of girlfriend does that make me?

261
15:11.465 --> 15:12.465
Come on, Miwa. Let's go.

262
15:32.705 --> 15:34.565
How long are you going to stay like that?

263
15:37.435 --> 15:38.435
Well...

264
15:46.845 --> 15:49.215
Aren't I still the one taking the lead here...?

265
15:51.885 --> 15:52.985
I'll try my best...

266
16:07.395 --> 16:08.695
Saeko...

267
16:10.265 --> 16:11.465
You're so cute.

268
16:29.485 --> 16:30.485
Sorry...

269
16:31.225 --> 16:33.105
I really can't take my clothes off after all...

270
16:34.895 --> 16:35.895
I understand.

271
16:36.585 --> 16:39.125
Then, can I touch you?

272
16:40.945 --> 16:41.945
It's okay.

273
17:15.665 --> 17:16.665
I'm sorry.

274
17:16.795 --> 17:17.805
Did I hurt you?

275
17:20.835 --> 17:21.835
No.

276
17:22.635 --> 17:23.935
It doesn't hurt, but...

277
17:25.445 --> 17:26.845
How do I put this...?

278
17:32.245 --> 17:34.285
You're just... really bad at this.

279
17:42.595 --> 17:43.595
Miwa.

280
17:43.825 --> 17:44.995
My turn.

281
17:45.625 --> 17:47.195
Wait, but...

282
17:47.595 --> 17:48.664
Tonight was supposed to be my...

283
17:48.665 --> 17:50.995
You're not ready for that level yet.

284
17:51.065 --> 17:52.065
What?

285
17:54.775 --> 17:55.775
Damn it...

286
18:03.475 --> 18:05.115
I'm pathetic...

287
18:12.765 --> 18:14.265
What am I even guarding against?

288
18:26.305 --> 18:27.634
Look, Miwa.

289
18:27.635 --> 18:28.635
Huh?

290
18:30.155 --> 18:31.155
Well?

291
18:31.305 --> 18:32.844
Aw, so cute!

292
18:32.845 --> 18:34.375
I'm going to wear this every day.

293
18:34.445 --> 18:35.445
Really?

294
18:35.446 --> 18:36.814
Even though you were so against it earlier?

295
18:36.815 --> 18:38.645
I wasn't against it.

296
18:38.685 --> 18:39.885
Just shy.

297
18:40.215 --> 18:41.085
Aww.

298
18:41.115 --> 18:42.115
Hey, look!

299
18:42.415 --> 18:45.425
Doesn't this make me look like Miwa's girl?

300
18:46.125 --> 18:47.525
What does that even mean?

301
18:51.925 --> 18:53.265
I'll be waiting for you...

302
19:17.105 --> 19:19.945
(Miwa: Sorry for not replying all day! I'm coming to the reunion, too!)

303
19:23.695 --> 19:24.695
It'll be fine...

304
19:26.825 --> 19:28.095
Why, why?

305
19:28.135 --> 19:29.135
What's going on?

306
19:30.175 --> 19:31.334
Oh, long time no see!

307
19:31.335 --> 19:32.865
Long time no see!

308
19:33.135 --> 19:34.604
Hey, long time no see!

309
19:34.605 --> 19:35.794
Sorry I'm late!

310
19:35.795 --> 19:37.454
Seriously, Miwa, you took forever!

311
19:37.455 --> 19:39.104
Sorry, the train was delayed...

312
19:39.105 --> 19:40.394
Oh, that explains it.

313
19:40.395 --> 19:41.675
Inuzuka?

314
19:51.725 --> 19:53.025
- Two! - Two!

315
19:55.755 --> 19:57.095
- Three! - Three!

316
20:00.265 --> 20:01.265
Hey, by the way...

317
20:01.795 --> 20:03.695
If we're talking about the boys' tennis team...

318
20:03.835 --> 20:05.005
...who do you like?

319
20:07.975 --> 20:08.975
Huh?

320
20:09.675 --> 20:10.854
Um...

321
20:10.855 --> 20:13.374
I don't really have a crush on anyone...

322
20:13.375 --> 20:14.645
If you had to pick one!

323
20:17.545 --> 20:21.085
Maybe Hachiya senpai?

324
20:21.185 --> 20:22.185
Oh?

325
20:22.255 --> 20:24.014
Hachiya senpai is great!

326
20:24.085 --> 20:25.361
You two would make a cute couple.

327
20:25.385 --> 20:27.085
You should go talk to him later.

328
20:27.755 --> 20:28.755
Oh...

329
20:28.995 --> 20:31.695
No, I didn't mean it like that...

330
20:32.495 --> 20:35.195
Everyone uses the word 'like'...

331
20:36.395 --> 20:38.875
...so why does it automatically turn into romantic feelings...

332
20:39.065 --> 20:41.705
...just because the person is a guy?

333
20:44.105 --> 20:46.705
Getting philosophical all of a sudden, huh?

334
20:47.475 --> 20:48.875
That kind of pressure...

335
20:49.445 --> 20:50.975
...it scares me a little.

336
20:53.755 --> 20:58.655
Why does romance make you feel like your life is being controlled by other people?

337
21:04.255 --> 21:06.195
You feel that way because...

338
21:07.465 --> 21:08.994
...it means you, Inuzuka...

339
21:08.995 --> 21:12.965
...haven't caved to the peer pressure of playing house with childish romance.

340
21:14.905 --> 21:16.935
Peer pressure...?

341
21:19.005 --> 21:20.605
You know how it is, right?

342
21:21.945 --> 21:23.745
My parents are really strict.

343
21:24.715 --> 21:26.144
Someone like me...

344
21:26.145 --> 21:28.655
...I've surrendered to all kinds of pressure so many times.

345
21:29.385 --> 21:33.155
Honestly, every day feels like hell.

346
21:35.375 --> 21:36.375
That's why...

347
21:38.465 --> 21:39.995
...out of everyone, you, Inuzuka...

348
21:41.165 --> 21:43.195
...I hope you never give in to that stuff.

349
21:49.505 --> 21:52.045
I've made up my mind.

350
21:53.345 --> 21:54.345
About what?

351
21:55.645 --> 21:59.715
My life...

352
22:00.045 --> 22:02.015
...I'm going to decide what makes me happy.

353
22:03.385 --> 22:06.055
No matter what anyone says, I won't give in.

354
22:06.225 --> 22:07.995
So Shiho senpai...

355
22:08.025 --> 22:09.355
...please don't give in, either.

356
22:09.695 --> 22:13.725
Let's find happiness on our own terms.

357
22:21.635 --> 22:22.635
The truth is...

358
22:23.675 --> 22:25.675
I came today specifically to see you, Inuzuka.

359
22:28.945 --> 22:30.715
What do you mean by that?

360
22:32.495 --> 22:33.495
What do I mean?

361
22:36.195 --> 22:41.325
Haven't you been avoiding me all this time?

362
22:42.495 --> 22:44.695
I thought you hated me.

363
22:47.795 --> 22:48.795
I'm sorry...

364
22:49.435 --> 22:50.995
I don't blame you...

365
22:54.195 --> 22:55.835
Right before graduation...

366
22:56.435 --> 22:58.675
...I was so overwhelmed by stuff with my family...

367
22:58.745 --> 23:00.975
...and stressed out over exams...

368
23:02.745 --> 23:04.625
...that I kept missing the chance to reach out.

369
23:05.485 --> 23:07.585
I just couldn't bring myself to text you...

370
23:12.255 --> 23:15.995
I never expected you to show up at the reunion.

371
23:19.425 --> 23:20.865
Did you not want to see me?

372
23:23.135 --> 23:24.135
Maybe...

373
23:26.275 --> 23:28.135
Maybe I didn't want to see you.

374
23:30.205 --> 23:32.005
But I really wanted to see you.

375
23:37.075 --> 23:38.585
That's so unfair...

376
23:50.515 --> 23:54.465
(Next Episode Preview) If the two of us work together, we can write the ultimate love song.

377
23:54.575 --> 23:56.434
I want us to go back to the way we were.

378
23:56.435 --> 23:58.805
What do you mean, 'the way we were'?

379
23:58.915 --> 23:59.915
This is...

380
23:59.916 --> 24:01.015
Ashida-san.

381
24:01.235 --> 24:02.605
We're not breaking up.

382
24:03.115 --> 24:04.115
Never.
